{"id": 1926404, "name": "WINDHAM v. LAFFERTY", "name_abbreviation": "Windham v. Lafferty", "decision_date": "1909-09-21", "docket_number": "7290", "first_page": "446", "last_page": "447", "citations": [{"type": "official", "cite": "83 S.C. 446"}], "court": {"name_abbreviation": "S.C.", "id": 8894, "name": "Supreme Court of South Carolina"}, "jurisdiction": {"id": 59, "name_long": "South Carolina", "name": "S.C."}, "cites_to": [{"cite": "72 S. C., 439", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "opinion_index": -1}, {"cite": "57 S. C., 293", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "opinion_index": -1}, {"cite": "54 S. C., 115", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [4409228], "opinion_index": -1, "case_paths": ["/sc/54/0115-01"]}, {"cite": "41 S. E., 299", "category": "reporters:state_regional", "reporter": "S.E.", "opinion_index": 0}, {"cite": "63 S. C., 366", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "opinion_index": 0}, {"cite": "35 S. E., 516", "category": "reporters:state_regional", "reporter": "S.E.", "opinion_index": 0}, {"cite": "57 S. C., 289", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [4412192], "opinion_index": 0, "case_paths": ["/sc/57/0289-01"]}, {"cite": "31 S. E., 885", "category": "reporters:state_regional", "reporter": "S.E.", "opinion_index": 0}, {"cite": "25 S. E., 296", "category": "reporters:state_regional", "reporter": "S.E.", "opinion_index": 0}, {"cite": "47 S. C., 446", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [4404212], "opinion_index": 0, "case_paths": ["/sc/47/0446-01"]}, {"cite": "22 S. C., 332", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [4382541], "opinion_index": 0, "case_paths": ["/sc/22/0332-01"]}, {"cite": "54 S. C., 115", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [4409228], "opinion_index": 0, "case_paths": ["/sc/54/0115-01"]}], "analysis": {"cardinality": 156, "char_count": 1572, "ocr_confidence": 0.63, "pagerank": {"raw": 4.947487136851577e-08, "percentile": 0.31073433238771836}, "sha256": "b9efed5a088d552c6b84fd4ea1633d69bc2bec4c621eec1dd16ec5e940fdfa88", "simhash": "1:6ff80c84fc5c72d3", "word_count": 282}, "last_updated": "2024-02-27T17:26:52.976801+00:00", "provenance": {"date_added": "2019-08-29", "source": "Harvard", "batch": "2018"}, "casebody": {"judges": [], "parties": ["WINDHAM v. LAFFERTY."], "opinions": [{"text": "The opinion of the Court was delivered by\nMr. Justice Hydricic.\nThis is an action for partition. Certain of the defendants set up an independent claim of title in themselves to the land sought to be partitioned. At the conclusion of the testimony offered by the plaintiffs, these defendants moved the Court for a nonsuit, which was granted, and judgment was entered accordingly.\nThis Court has frequently decided that it is error to grant a nonsuit in such a case. Woolfolk v. Graniteville, 22 S. C., 332; McClenaghan v. McEachern, 47 S. C., 446, 25 S. E., 296; Barnes v. Rodgers, 54 S. C., 115, 31 S. E., 885; Gilreath v. Furman, 57 S. C., 289, 35 S. E., 516; Railway v. Beaudrot, 63 S. C., 366, 41 S. E., 299.\nIf the party claiming partition offers no testimony tending to establish his claim, a motion to direct the verdict is the proper remedy. Barnes v. Rodgers, and Gilreath v. Furman, supra.\nThe judgment of nonsuit is reversed and a new trial granted.", "type": "majority", "author": "Mr. Justice Hydricic."}], "attorneys": ["Messrs. B. O. Woods and Stevenson & Matheson, for appellant.", "Messrs. Geo. W. Brown and Shand & Shand, contra."], "corrections": "", "head_matter": "7290\nWINDHAM v. LAFFERTY.\nNonsuit. \u2014 In an action for partition where an issue of title has been raised by answer, on the trial of this issue by a jury, it is improper to grant nonsuit.\nBefore Aldrich, J., Darlington, Spring term, 1908.\nReversed.\nAction by Mary N. Windham et al. against Cordelia Lafferty et al. From order of nonsuit, plaintiff appeals.\nMessrs. B. O. Woods and Stevenson & Matheson, for appellant.\nMr. Woods cites: On question decided: 54 S. C., 115; 57 S. C., 293; 63 S. C\u201e 270; 72 S. C., 439.\nMessrs. Geo. W. Brown and Shand & Shand, contra.\nNo citation on point decided.\nSeptember 21, 1909."}, "file_name": "0446-01", "first_page_order": 460, "last_page_order": 461}